# SRG-APP-000065-AU-000240  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must enforce the limit of three consecutive invalid
# logon attempts by a user during a 15 minute time period.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000065-AU-000240
group:           V-221904
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000044
control_rev5:    AC-7

contribution:    Splunk's native authentication counts failed logons per user and locks the
                 account itself; whether lockout is enabled, how many attempts trigger it,
                 and the window over which attempts are counted are all application
                 settings in authentication.conf [splunk_auth].

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutUsers in 1|true
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutAttempts max 3
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutThresholdMins min 15
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutAttempts min 1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutThresholdMins max 120
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutAttempts https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutThresholdMins https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] lockoutUsers https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        These settings govern Splunk-native accounts only. Where users
                 authenticate through LDAP, SAML or a scripted provider, the
                 consecutive-invalid-attempt limit is enforced by that provider and is
                 assessed under its own baseline.
external:        Per authentication.conf.spec:517-518, lockout state on a search head
                 cluster member applies to that member only and not to the cluster, so a
                 limit spanning the cluster is not expressible in Splunk configuration.

citation:        CHANGED for INVENTION. The condition 'authentication.conf [splunk_auth]
                 lockoutMins present' has been removed. lockoutMins is the lockout
                 duration, the number of minutes a user stays locked out after the limit is
                 reached (authentication.conf.spec:521-530, default 30). This requirement
                 is CCI-000044 / AC-7 a, the limit on consecutive invalid attempts; the
                 duration of the lockout is a different control enhancement and belongs to
                 the requirement that addresses it. The operand appears in neither the SRG
                 check text nor the product STIG fix text for SPLK-CL-000060, whose fix
                 sets only lockoutAttempts and lockoutThresholdMins, and because
                 lockoutMins has a default it reads as present in every merged
                 configuration, so the condition can never fail and adds no evidence while
                 attributing another requirement's objective to this row. The two numeric
                 directions were checked against the product STIG check text and are
                 correct as written and retained: lockoutAttempts takes max:3 because more
                 than 3 is a finding, lockoutThresholdMins takes min:15 because less than
                 15 is a finding, and each correctly fails the vendor default of 5
                 (authentication.conf.spec:541, :552). lockoutUsers is retained on the
                 specification's own terms, since authentication.conf.spec:514-519 makes it
                 the switch that gives the other two settings effect, and in:1|true accepts
                 either boolean spelling.
finding:         Splunk-native authentication is not configured to lock an account after
                 three consecutive invalid logon attempts within a 15 minute window, so the
                 application is not configured to the extent the product allows toward the
                 attempt limit.
